title: Ask-user picker trusts only contentHash-verified structured detail; answer binding is an accepted cached-class risk
summary: 'card:v1 has no detail field, so the kernel carries the validated questions in one ask-user block node holding the exact hashed detail; the GUI recomputes contentHash (contracts sha256 + canonicalJson) and builds the picker only on a match, so display text is never parsed. Aegis C3 resolved as option (b): approveMessage is kernel-local (not a clientApiId input), but the helper signs what the kernel received, so binding noteHash would not stop a frame rewriter who can already flip a cached deny; recorded in spec 3.4, batched into T-2026-10-19-001.'
